method:
Zero searches. spp-jpp.org/icpp links http://www.icpp-spp.org/index.php, whose front page offers 'download: Scientific Program' (img_icpp14/ICPP14_Program_web.pdf, 148 pp, 19.8 MB) and 'download: Book of Abstracts' (img_icpp14/ICPP14_BoA_web.pdf) for ICPP-14, Kyoto, 28 June-3 July 2026. Worked the Scientific Program. POSTERS: printed pp 69-98 = PDF pp 91-120 ('Poster Session 1 - Tuesday' / 'Poster Session 2 - Thursday'); extracted with pdftotext -layout and -raw; board codes are printed rotated so some come out letter-spaced ('S 2 9 - 0 2'), so matched S\s?\d\s?\d\s?-\s?\d\s?\d(\s?\d)? and stripped whitespace -> 185 unique (layout; 3 gaps) / 187 (raw; noisy). TALKS: every talk is a 'HH:MM to HH:MM <label>' slot; regex (\d\d:\d\d to \d\d:\d\d)[ 	]*([^
]*)
\s*([^
]*) over the -layout text -> 359 slots labelled 'Invited Lecture' (EXCLUDED as invited), 40 unlabelled slots whose next line is a presenter with affiliation in parentheses (counted as contributed - e.g. session '42. Contributed - Materials'), 60 other (coffee, lunch, ceremonies, award lectures). COUNTED contributed = 185 + ~40 = ~225; the talk-slot split is a single-extraction heuristic, hence confidence 'derived'. ATTENDANCE: the same PDF's 'Participants by Country' (PDF pp 121-126) lists 552 unique delegate names (regex ^[^\d,]{1,40}, [^\d,]{1,40}$ on -raw text, which excludes the page-numbered author index). Language searched: English (SPP publishes in English; the Kyoto host did not publish a separate Japanese programme on this site). VERDICT: every reading - 225 contributed, or ~585 if all invited talks were counted too - is positive evidence below the 800 near-bar threshold and the ~900 floor: OUT. Rung 9 not needed.
